 "title_latin": "Koga padna na Pirina",
 "title_en": "When he fell at Pirin",
 "pesna_url": "https://pesna.org/song/463",
 "background": "A ballad of the wounded Jane Sandanski, built as a dialogue. Three falcons descend and urge him to come with them to Pirin, to the white sea and to the Vardar, because Mother Macedonia will find a cure for such a hero. His answer: I am wounded in the heart, leave me here to die, no cure cures me; Macedonia will bear others who will free her. The song compresses myth and history the way folk songs do.",
 "background_source": "Source of these notes: Qwen's draft.",
 "english_kind": "pesna",
